  "content": {
    "id": "p19-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "An object moves according to $x=\\dfrac{e^{t-0.1t^3}}{2}$, where $x$ is its displacement in metres and $t$ is time in seconds.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p19-q11-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find its displacement and velocity at $t=2$ seconds. Give displacement to 2 decimal places and velocity to 3 decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x(2)\\approx1.66\\text{ m}$; $v(2)\\approx-0.332\\text{ m/s}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x(2)&=\\frac{e^{2-0.1(2)^3}}{2}\\\\&=\\frac{e^{1.2}}{2}\\\\&\\approx1.66\\text{ m}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}v(t)=\\frac{dx}{dt}&=\\frac{(1-0.3t^2)e^{t-0.1t^3}}{2}\\\\v(2)&=\\frac{(1-0.3(2)^2)e^{1.2}}{2}\\\\&=-0.1e^{1.2}\\\\&\\approx-0.332\\text{ m/s}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q11-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "What happens to its displacement and velocity as $t\\to\\infty$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Displacement and velocity both approach $0$.",
          "worked": "As $t\\to\\infty$, $t-0.1t^3\\to-\\infty$, so\n$$\\begin{align*}x(t)&=\\frac{e^{t-0.1t^3}}{2}\\\\&\\to0\\text{ m}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe exponential factor tends to zero faster than the quadratic factor grows, so\n$$\\begin{align*}v(t)&=\\frac{(1-0.3t^2)e^{t-0.1t^3}}{2}\\\\&\\to0\\text{ m/s}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      }
    ]
  },
